<title>POLAND: POLL-Polish 52-wk,13-wk T-bill yield seen down.</title>
<headline>POLL-Polish 52-wk,13-wk T-bill yield seen down.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banks expect the average yield on Poland's benchmark 52-week T-bill to fall to 20.12 percent at the end of 1997 against 21.86 percent at last week's primary sale, a Reuters poll of the country's 25 largest banks showed.</p>
<p>The average yield on the 13-week T-bill was also seen falling to 19.61 percent by year-end from 21.13 percent at Monday's primary auction, the poll showed.</p>
<p>But both predictions were higher than a month ago.</p>
<p>		    JULY	   END-97	  12-MONTHS AHEAD</p>
<p> 52-WEEK AVG   21.96	20.12 (18.66)     18.37 (17.41)</p>
<p>     MINIMUM   21.30	14.90 (16.30)     13.20 (14.40)</p>
<p>     MAXIMUM   22.25	22.00 (20.60)     21.50 (19.80)</p>
<p> 13-WEEK AVG   21.37	19.61 (18.27)     17.88 (16.95)</p>
<p>     MINIMUM   21.00	14.00 (16.20)     12.00 (14.10)</p>
<p>     MAXIMUM   21.85	22.00 (20.30)     21.00 (19.50)</p>
<p>NOTE: In brackets previous figures for end-97 and June-98 from last month's poll.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
